# Base recommends for Lotus OS with --apt-recommends false
# live-build applies that flag to ALL apt installs (not just GNOME).
# Depends still install; Recommends do not — this file puts back packages that
# would otherwise leave the live image / desktop / tools broken or half-working.
#
# Sources: live-manual §apt-recommends, live-boot/live-config Recommends on
# Trixie, and Recommends of network-manager / gdm3 / gnome-shell /
# gnome-settings-daemon / podman / apt / git / nautilus.
#
# Already covered by "! Packages Priority standard" in standard.list.chroot
# (do not need to repeat): locales, ca-certificates, libpam-systemd,
# systemd-timesyncd, openssh-client, pciutils, iproute2, less,
# linux-sysctl-defaults, …
#
# Intentionally omitted (bloat / niche): live-*-doc, locales-all, rygel,
# gnome-user-docs, cups*, gnome-remote-desktop, buildah, criu,
# switcheroo-control, xserver-xephyr.

# --- Live boot/config (CRITICAL — live-manual names these explicitly) ---
# Without user-setup: no live user → cannot log in.
# Without sudo: live user cannot shut down / elevate (also listed in standard).
user-setup
sudo
live-tools
# live-config keyboard component expects console-setup (+ keyboard-configuration).
console-setup
keyboard-configuration
# live-boot recommends — UUID/rsync used by live tooling; eject for media/Nautilus.
uuid-runtime
rsync
eject

# --- NetworkManager stack (Wi-Fi / policykit break if missing) ---
# NM Recommends on Trixie: wpasupplicant, wireless-regdb, dnsmasq-base, …
wpasupplicant
wireless-regdb
dnsmasq-base
polkitd
# Advanced connection editor (gnome-control-center also recommends this).
nm-connection-editor
network-manager-l10n
# Optional but common on laptops; small cost vs. broken WWAN/tethering.
modemmanager
mobile-broadband-provider-info
ppp

# --- Session / privilege / user bus ---
# dbus-user-session: GNOME portals, PipeWire, rootless podman (libpam-systemd Rec).
# pkexec: gnome-settings-daemon Rec — GUI privilege prompts.
dbus-user-session
pkexec

# --- GNOME soft deps that are Recommends (shell/settings feel broken without) ---
# EDS daemon: gnome-shell Rec (calendar/clock integration).
evolution-data-server
# IME: gnome-shell Rec; with recommends false also pull GTK frontends.
ibus
ibus-gtk
ibus-gtk3
ibus-gtk4
im-config
# # Uncomment for Vietnamese typing:
# ibus-unikey
power-profiles-daemon
iio-sensor-proxy
bolt
x11-xserver-utils
x11-xkb-utils
iso-codes
cracklib-runtime
libnss-myhostname
gnome-bluetooth-sendto
# Nautilus Rec — thumbnails / SVG / Space preview.
libgdk-pixbuf2.0-bin
librsvg2-common
gnome-sushi
# gdm3 Rec — Xorg stack helps on hardware where Wayland is flaky; Xwayland
# already comes in via gnome-session Depends.
xserver-xorg

# --- Podman (standard.list) Recommends needed for rootless use ---
uidmap
catatonit
passt
containers-storage

# --- TLS / VCS helpers often only Recommends ---
# ca-certificates is Priority:standard (already via standard.list) — listed
# here so base stays correct if that line is ever removed.
ca-certificates
patch
bash-completion

# --- Storage / USB / fonts commonly expected on a live workstation ---
fuse3
ntfs-3g
dosfstools
usbutils
fonts-dejavu-core
fonts-noto-color-emoji

# --- Optional hardware helpers (safe; enable if you want firmware GUI) ---
# fwupd
# switcheroo-control
